# Koh, the Face Stealer (CR 607.2a, 607.5): Koh's enters trigger exiles one of Bot2's Emperors of Bones on turn 3, and its dies
# trigger exiles the other, which Bot1's Lightning Bolt kills on turn 5. Bot1 pays 1 life to choose the first Emperor, and at the
# beginning of combat that card's lent trigger exiles the Llanowar Elves Bot2's Shock killed. In the second main phase Bot1 pays
# again and chooses the same Emperor, which was the last chosen card all along: nothing stopped lending it, so Koh has the same
# abilities of it as before. Bot1 adapts with its lent "{1}{B}: Adapt 2", and the lent "put a creature card exiled with this
# creature onto the battlefield", linked to the lent exile ability, puts the Elves onto the battlefield with a finality counter.

